{"landed-cost": "\n    <h1>Landed Cost Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Find the true cost of an imported part once freight, insurance, duty and customs fees are added. Example values are filled in; replace them with your shipment.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-price\">Unit price (FOB) <span class=\"u\">per unit</span></label><input id=\"lc-price\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"4.20\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-qty\">Quantity <span class=\"u\">units</span></label><input id=\"lc-qty\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"5000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-freight\">Freight <span class=\"u\">shipment total</span></label><input id=\"lc-freight\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"1850\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-ins\">Insurance <span class=\"u\">% of goods</span></label><input id=\"lc-ins\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-duty\">Duty rate <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"lc-duty\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"6.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-fees\">Customs &amp; broker fees <span class=\"u\">total</span></label><input id=\"lc-fees\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"320\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-other\">Port, handling, inland <span class=\"u\">total</span></label><input id=\"lc-other\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"410\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label>Duty charged on</label>\n          <div class=\"seg\" id=\"lc-basis\"><button type=\"button\" data-b=\"cif\" aria-pressed=\"true\">CIF value</button><button type=\"button\" data-b=\"fob\" aria-pressed=\"false\">FOB value</button></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Landed cost per unit</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"lc-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"lc-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"lc-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"lc-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"lc-tbl\"></table>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><p>Landed cost is everything you pay to get goods onto your shop floor. The purchase price is only the start.</p>\n      <code class=\"fx\">Customs value = goods + freight + insurance  (CIF)\nDuty         = customs value × duty rate\nLanded cost  = goods + freight + insurance\n             + duty + fees + handling</code></div>\n      <div><h2>CIF or FOB?</h2><p>The EU, UK, Korea, China and most other countries charge duty on the CIF value, which includes freight and insurance. The US and Canada charge duty on the FOB value, so freight is left out of the duty base.</p><p>Duty rates come from the HS code of your product. Check your country's tariff schedule before you quote a price.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "cost-per-good-unit": "\n    <h1>Cost per Good Unit Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Every rejected part still used material, labor and machine time. This spreads that cost over the parts you can actually ship.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-mat\">Material cost <span class=\"u\">per unit started</span></label><input id=\"cg-mat\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"2.80\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-conv\">Labor + overhead <span class=\"u\">per unit started</span></label><input id=\"cg-conv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"1.65\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-start\">Units started <span class=\"u\">per batch</span></label><input id=\"cg-start\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"12000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-yield\">First-pass yield <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"cg-yield\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"91.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"cg-salv\">Scrap salvage value <span class=\"u\">per rejected unit</span></label><input id=\"cg-salv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0.15\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Cost per good unit</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"cg-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"cg-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"cg-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"cg-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"cg-tbl\"></table>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Good units   = units started × yield\nTotal cost   = started × (material + conversion)\n             − rejects × salvage\nCost / good  = total cost ÷ good units</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Why yield matters</h2><p>At 90% yield, each good part carries the cost of about 1.11 parts. Raising yield from 90% to 95% cuts that to 1.05, which lowers unit cost by about 5% without touching material prices.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "scrap-cost": "\n    <h1>Scrap &amp; Rework Cost Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Put a yearly number on quality losses so an improvement project can be justified in money, not percentages.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-vol\">Production volume <span class=\"u\">units / month</span></label><input id=\"sc-vol\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"40000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-cost\">Full cost per unit <span class=\"u\">at scrap point</span></label><input id=\"sc-cost\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"6.40\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-scrap\">Scrap rate <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"sc-scrap\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"3.2\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-salv\">Salvage value <span class=\"u\">per scrapped unit</span></label><input id=\"sc-salv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0.40\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-rw\">Rework rate <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"sc-rw\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"4.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-rwc\">Rework cost <span class=\"u\">per reworked unit</span></label><input id=\"sc-rwc\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"1.90\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"sc-target\">Target scrap rate after improvement <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"sc-target\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"1.5\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Quality loss per year</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"sc-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"sc-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"sc-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"sc-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"sc-tbl\"></table>\n        <div id=\"sc-pill\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Scrap loss  = volume × scrap % × (cost − salvage)\nRework loss = volume × rework % × rework cost\nYearly loss = (scrap + rework) × 12</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Which unit cost to use</h2><p>Use the full cost the part has absorbed at the step where it is scrapped. A part rejected at final inspection carries every operation before it, so it costs more than one rejected at incoming inspection.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "break-even": "\n    <h1>Break-Even Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">How many units you need to sell each month before the product starts making money.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-fixed\">Fixed costs <span class=\"u\">per month</span></label><input id=\"be-fixed\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"28000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-price\">Selling price <span class=\"u\">per unit</span></label><input id=\"be-price\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"24\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-var\">Variable cost <span class=\"u\">per unit</span></label><input id=\"be-var\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"13.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-target\">Target profit <span class=\"u\">per month</span></label><input id=\"be-target\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"8000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"be-sales\">Expected sales <span class=\"u\">units / month</span></label><input id=\"be-sales\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"3500\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Break-even volume</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"be-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"be-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"be-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"be-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"be-tbl\"></table>\n        <div id=\"be-pill\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Contribution  = price − variable cost\nBreak-even    = fixed costs ÷ contribution\nTarget volume = (fixed + target) ÷ contribution\nSafety margin = (expected − break-even) ÷ expected</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Fixed vs variable</h2><p>Fixed costs stay the same whatever you produce: rent, salaried staff, leases, depreciation. Variable costs rise with each unit: material, piece-rate labor, packaging, sales commission and shipping.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "payback": "\n    <h1>Equipment Payback &amp; ROI Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Test whether a new machine, fixture or automation cell pays for itself, and how fast.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-inv\">Investment <span class=\"u\">purchase + install</span></label><input id=\"pb-inv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"185000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-life\">Useful life <span class=\"u\">years</span></label><input id=\"pb-life\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"7\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-labor\">Labor savings <span class=\"u\">per year</span></label><input id=\"pb-labor\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"52000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-qual\">Scrap / quality savings <span class=\"u\">per year</span></label><input id=\"pb-qual\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"14000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-op\">Added running cost <span class=\"u\">power, upkeep / year</span></label><input id=\"pb-op\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"9500\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-rate\">Discount rate <span class=\"u\">% / year</span></label><input id=\"pb-rate\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"8\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Simple payback</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"pb-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"pb-sub\"></div>\n        <svg id=\"pb-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 120\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cumulative cash flow by year\" style=\"margin-top:14px;max-width:100%\"></svg>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"pb-tbl\"></table>\n        <div id=\"pb-pill\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Net saving = labor + quality − running cost\nPayback    = investment ÷ net saving\nROI        = (net saving × life − investment)\n             ÷ investment\nNPV        = Σ net saving ÷ (1+r)^t − investment</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Reading the result</h2><p>Many plants approve projects that pay back in under 2–3 years. NPV is the stricter test: a positive NPV means the machine earns more than leaving the money at your discount rate.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  "}